{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>An east wind.</b> A noun of description, for eastward is in front, and it is called קדים because it is frontward among the directions, for from there the sun begins to shine. Therefore west is called אחור, like 'in front I walk, but He is not, and backward, but I cannot perceive Him' (Job 23:8)." "<b>He carried the locusts.</b> From their place, and deposited them in all the land of Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:16.451617135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}